{"message":"For a 3-month trip, the Green Fee-Free Account appears to be the lowest-cost personal checking option based on the available fee information: $0 Rho-Bank fee for foreign ATM withdrawals and $0 for out-of-network ATM withdrawals. Its $22.50 monthly maintenance fee is waived if you maintain a minimum daily balance of $150, so keeping that balance would avoid $67.50 over three months. Foreign ATM operator surcharges may still apply, and the daily ATM withdrawal limit is $500.

The Bluest Account also has no Rho-Bank foreign ATM fee and rebates foreign ATM operator fees up to $50 per monthly statement cycle, but I don’t have its monthly maintenance-fee terms, so I can’t confirm that it would cost less overall. For either account, choose to be charged in the local currency rather than accepting the ATM’s currency conversion when prompted.

If you’d like to open the Green Fee-Free Account, please confirm that you can maintain at least $150 daily and that you want this specific account."}

{"message":"Not categorically. Assuming you maintain the $150 daily balance, Green Fee-Free is the safest low-cost choice among the personal accounts whose full fee terms are available: its $22.50 monthly fee is waived, and Rho charges $0 for foreign ATM withdrawals. Over three months, your Rho fees could therefore be $0, aside from any ATM operator surcharges.

However, it does not reimburse those operator surcharges. If you expect to use ATMs that charge substantial fees, Bluest could be cheaper because it has no Rho foreign-ATM fee and rebates third-party ATM fees up to $50 per month, but its monthly maintenance-fee terms were not provided, so I can’t confirm its total cost. Purple also rebates operator fees up to $30 monthly, but its $15 monthly fee is waived only with a $3,750 minimum daily balance.

So: choose Green Fee-Free if you can use low-surcharge ATMs or want a predictable $150 balance requirement. Bluest may be better if you expect more than $50 per month in eligible operator fees and its account-level fees are acceptable. In all cases, ATM operator fees and currency-conversion costs can still affect the total."}
